# Base URL of the simple-auth API this app talks to, with no trailing slash
# (e.g. https://api.example.com). Leave unset/empty to use relative paths —
# that's correct for local dev (Vite's proxy in vite.config.js forwards them
# to simple-auth) and for a production deployment where this app is served
# from the exact same origin as simple-auth.
#
# If simple-auth is deployed on a different origin, set this. It must still
# share a parent domain with wherever this app is hosted (e.g.
# app.example.com talking to VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com) — the
# refresh-token cookie simple-auth sets is SameSite=Strict, which browsers
# never send across unrelated domains no matter what this is set to. See the
# README for details.
VITE_API_URL=
